WEBVTT

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.360
Her fever isn't coming down.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.210
We don't have any medicine, either.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.690
At this rate...

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.200
Hazu-nee...

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.130
Haa-nee...

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.110
Haa-nee!

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:21.560
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:21.560
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:29.360
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:29.360
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:36.610
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:36.610
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.700
shinkuromanika

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.700
Synchromanica

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.240
itsu no ma ni ka

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.240
Before I know it

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.410
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.410
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:49.710
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:49.710
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:56.220
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:56.220
I can hear someone's dream

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:03.180
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:03.180
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.990
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.990
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.320
shinkuromanika

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.320
Synchromanica

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.450
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.450
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.490
shinkuromanika

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.490
Synchromanica

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.710
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.710
The synchrony of your life

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.050
Galileo Tesoro

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.490
Happy eleventh birthday, Roberto.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:46.020
Happy birthday.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.270
Thank you

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.150
Papa, Mama!

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.330
Hey, you need to leave!

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.150
Please give us food.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.320
We haven't had a decent meal in two days...

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.530
You want us to die?

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.070
Hey!

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:01.490
Cut it out!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:04.170
Don't be so heartless, man.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.830
Wow, this is amazing...

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.540
Are you sure about giving so much?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.360
Sorry...

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:18.450
Please help yourselves.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.870
It's delicious!

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:25.980
<i>Everyone has an equal right to life.</i>

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.220
<i>If you have more than others,</i>

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.130
<i>you should share with those who have less.</i>

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.230
<i>If you feel happier than others,</i>

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.710
<i>help those who are in need.</i>

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:42.470
<i>That is the duty of those who are given so much.</i>

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:49.750
Sorry...

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.120
This is all that's left.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:58.520
There!

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:02.760
Now we can all have some.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.350
Let's eat!

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:07.750
Right.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:48.600
Papa!

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.760
Run, Roberto...

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:55.440
If the rest collapses, you'll also be...

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.190
No! I can't!

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.410
Wait, Papa...

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.440
I'll save you.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.120
I'll get you out!

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:04.190
It's no use, Roberto.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:05.740
You're only a child.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.050
Damn, this is bad.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.050
Someone's here!

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:12.370
Hang on.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:15.340
Please help!

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.330
Papa's... Papa's...

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.850
Your papa?

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:20.790
Hey, look...

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.800
Huh?

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.970
What are you doing?

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.060
Help me!

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.720
Papa will die!

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.810
Oh, shut up!

00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.190
Wait, please...

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:40.770
Come back!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.780
Papa...

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.440
Papa!

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.310
What an insignificant dream.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.010
Hospital located!

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.440
Hurry!

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.480
Let's gun it.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.430
Need to get shots for her...

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:21.020
Let's get Hazuki shots and meds, ASAP!

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:41.490
We may be wanted fugitives,
but should we really be stealing medicine?

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.040
We shouldn't, but Haa-nee's in trouble...

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:47.050
I don't want to lose her!

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.960
Well, yeah.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.760
Isn't it too quiet?

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:11.200
What is this?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.590
What's going on?

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:18.010
What are <i>you</i> guys doing here?

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:19.120
BlaGany-san?

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:20.090
Don't shorten it!

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:22.640
You don't deserve our respect!

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.960
Why are you here?

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.040
Don't move!

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.340
Stop right there.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:30.220
The Black Ganymede Association has taken possession of this hospital!

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:30.920
Yeah!

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:33.180
Huh? Why?

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:36.680
Marco!

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:41.060
Due to the fierce blizzard outside,
I am stranded here.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:44.240
Furthermore, the damage done to the thrusters

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.570
makes the Aza Iron's launch ability dubious.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:52.570
Given the circumstances,
I have no choice but to strip usable parts

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:55.570
from the hospital's air-fish to repair the engines.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.530
You're...

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:01.500
A brief stop to seize parts and avoid the blizzard.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.010
That is the point of this takeover.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:07.790
It's nauseating to think that I must take the same action as you.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.170
You're Roberto Materrazzi!

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:13.550
I'll be in control of this hospital now.

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.590
Your job here is finished.

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.640
What?

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.310
Ow!

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.720
Damn it!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:25.890
I said that you're not needed here, Black Ganymede.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:28.730
Not that that's anything new.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:30.730
Are you okay?

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:36.680
You've been dead from the moment you stole that methane hydrate from Adnimoon.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:39.990
You should be grateful for lasting this long.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.750
Mama...

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:43.750
Oh, yeah...

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.000
We're grateful, all right.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:49.130
For the countless stars that'll still be shining down on us tomorrow.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.970
Not bad... For a rich, spoiled brat.

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:05.390
I've at least got the strength to squash pests!

00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:08.150
I'll try to live up to your expectations!

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.650
Lead bullets and pests go hand-in-hand.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:15.030
They suit you, too.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:32.290
Hozuki-chan, have you found the medicine yet?

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:33.630
Huh?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.010
Hey, roller-hair girl...

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.600
You're staring like you're his girlfriend.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:46.850
Let's go!

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.020
Stop right there, roller-hair girl.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.680
Just go...

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:54.710
Hurry!

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.920
Here! Found it!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:08.920
Whew.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.380
This'll save Haa-nee...

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.920
Save it for later. Let's go.

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:14.250
What about Anna-san?

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:17.170
We can come back for her once we get the meds to Haa-nee—

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:27.020
It seems the generator malfunctioned.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:30.120
Who knows how long backup power will hold out?

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.120
Talk about bad luck...

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:36.780
You guys are unlucky too, coming here at a time like this.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.820
I have to get back soon.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:39.910
Hazuki-chan's...

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:41.660
What?

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.120
No, it isn't working.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.740
Let's try circling around from outside.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:46.790
That won't work.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.460
The blizzard's worsened.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.670
We can't go outside...

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:51.460
Then what?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.680
We finally got the meds!

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:57.760
BlaGany, you should really lay off.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:58.800
Outta the way!

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:04.550
Push!

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.850
Why?

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.920
The boss ordered it.

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:15.690
Don't you need to get back to save your big sister?

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:21.960
Kakkii...

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.950
Hocchii...

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:30.460
Bambina...

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.000
Don't give me that!

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:34.240
I said to turn on the heater.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.680
We're all gonna freeze to death!

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:39.840
I already told you, the backup power isn't enough...

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.160
Well, the second floor's all lit up.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.260
Just reroute that power here!

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:46.260
We can't do that!

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:49.270
The second floor houses many critically ill patients.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:53.230
They need electrical medical equipment to stay alive!

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:56.260
So you're saying they're more important?

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.610
That's discrimination!

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.320
Yeah, discrimination!

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:02.990
Why should we have to suffer for them?

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:05.370
Even if you're a doctor, don't push it!

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.700
You want to die?

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.030
I've got money!

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:09.240
Save us instead!

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.160
They're already good as dead, anyway.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.210
Isn't saving us more important?

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.750
This hospital chooses who to save?

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.710
No, that isn't true!

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:17.750
We'd never...

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.770
Hey, keep quiet!

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:21.630
Behave yourselves!

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.880
We've already been waiting five hours.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.550
We'll sue you later!

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.350
This hospital sucks.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:29.600
Are you guys telling me to die?

00:12:53.690 --> 00:12:55.580
I like the look in your eyes...

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:01.090
From this day forward, you'll be my son.

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:20.330
This looks hopeless.

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.440
BlaGany-san, you're bleeding!

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.490
This is nothing...

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.900
Why would you go out of your way for us?

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:29.990
Boss's orders...

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:37.080
We're all prepared to throw away our lives for the boss if we must.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.750
Compared to that, this is just a scratch!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:44.920
You guys are stupid, doing that for a flippant moron like him.

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:47.510
You don't know anything about him!

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:53.360
All of us in Black Ganymede were orphans.

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:57.020
In this day and age, parents abandoning their kids isn't out of the ordinary...

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.060
Our orphanage was crap.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:04.030
The adults vented their stress on the kids.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:05.320
No way!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:10.340
They beat us for the slightest mistake, even during meals and baths.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:14.580
They probably just wanted to dominate the weak.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:18.580
Then he showed up.

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.510
You guys make me sick!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:28.080
I'm sure he didn't like anyone who wanted to oppress others.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.190
But he saved our lives...

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:35.070
He's a man we can follow.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:43.370
More of us felt that way, and before you knew it,

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:45.980
we'd become a big group.

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.850
The boss gave us our freedom...

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:57.790
That's why following his orders

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.170
proves that we are free men.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.420
You just <i>think</i> that.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.940
What kind of freedom is that?

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:06.550
Becoming air pirates and stealing other people's stuff?

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.090
Those are just crimes!

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.990
So parents abandoning their kids is okay?

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:13.580
What about those meds?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.010
Did you pay for them?

00:15:16.830 --> 00:15:21.050
There aren't enough resources or energy to go around.

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:23.360
You have to steal to live.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:25.300
That's just how it is.

00:15:25.300 --> 00:15:27.690
You steal because there's no other way to survive.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:31.400
Just like abandoning your own kids... And everything else!

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:34.660
Hocchibi?

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:37.370
It doesn't have to be that way.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.560
That's just too sad...

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:46.540
Why do people need to suffer? It's not anyone's fault.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:51.680
Why does the world have to work this way?

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:58.260
That isn't a problem we can fix.

00:15:58.260 --> 00:15:59.600
But...

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.860
I'll answer your demands.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.190
Die.

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:11.780
You bastard!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:14.780
Damn, you don't do things halfway.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:18.280
Your execution will have to wait.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:20.040
What the—

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.260
Roberto, stop!

00:16:35.630 --> 00:16:40.890
Most human beings are hideous and filled with greed.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.690
The reprehensible ones taint the dignity of the others.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:48.150
They will devour, consume and kill.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:51.970
They do not deserve to live.

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:54.650
No, they must die.

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:56.660
They must be killed...

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:58.240
By someone.

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.250
By someone...

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:06.600
By <i>me</i>.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:09.840
You make me sick.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:14.590
Why do you get to decide who should die?

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:18.510
Why do they need <i>your</i> permission to live?!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.940
Humanity is too numerous.

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:22.690
With respect to our numbers,

00:17:22.690 --> 00:17:25.140
the world's capacity to support us is overly strained.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:30.400
There simply isn't enough energy to go around.

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:34.570
Essentially, I am the world's spokesman.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.950
If one side of the balance becomes too heavy, you could say that

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:40.660
removing some weight is my responsibility.

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:43.910
That isn't right.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:48.160
Thus, even hideous souls can be transformed into martyrs.

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:49.420
My actions

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.920
are salvation.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.770
Salvation?

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:58.930
Why? Why did Theo have to be sacrificed?

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.720
That's the kind of arrogance that grates on my nerves!

00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:07.520
Kiara!

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:09.270
Hang in there!

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:14.800
Damn...

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.710
I don't want this anymore...

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.030
Please stop!

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:33.430
Hocchibi!

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:57.320
This...

00:18:58.220 --> 00:18:59.810
This light...

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:08.830
It's so warm...

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:46.450
Oh, Haa-nee!

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:47.990
Kaa-nee!

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.410
Anna-san!

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:54.010
The blizzard's died down!

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:55.500
We can go out now.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:56.920
Let's go!

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:02.420
Anna-san?

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:03.280
Huh?

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.060
Oh...

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:05.510
L-Let's go.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.830
Haa-nee, we brought meds!

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:18.560
I'm not a fan

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:20.650
of powdered meds.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.590
Moron.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:25.480
We're leaving now.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:26.740
We have to get out of here!

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.240
Goody goody goldfish!

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.370
Nice weather, isn't it?

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:33.250
Now Hazuki will get better!

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:56.730
Seems luck is in your favor.

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:15.090
I've found you, Galileo Tesoro!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
